-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Question 1 : Kyun synchronous communication galat approach hai notification process karne ke liye?
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Upstream Service
    │
    ├── Template DB se fetch karo
    ├── Template populate karo
    ├── SMS Provider REST API call karo
    └── Response ka wait karo... (thread blocked)

    Problems :

    1. Tight Coupling
       Tight coupling ka matlab — upstream service provider-specific details (URL, timeout, retry, response format) khud handle kar rahi hai. 
       Provider change ho, naya provider add ho (naya channel add hone par) — har case me upstream service ka code change karna padega.

    2. Thread Blocking
       REST call synchronous hai — upstream service ka thread provider ke response ka wait karta hai. Us duration me wo thread kuch aur nahi kar sakta.

    3. Cascading Failure
       Provider down hai → upstream service retries karti hai → retries fail → upstream service bhi fail ho jaati hai. Ek non-critical cheez (notification)
       critical service (Order) ko down kar deti hai.

    4. High Traffic Pe Collapse
       Bulk notifications (10K users ko ek saath) → har notification ke liye thread block → thread pool exhaust → nayi requests ke liye koi thread nahi → system hang.
   
    

