      i) Channel-wise Event Publishing & Processing

         - Ab Instance 1 producer ki tarah act karta hai aur 3 alag Kafka topics (email_events, sms_events aur push_events) mein respective payloads/events publish karta hai.

         - Har topic ka apna independent Consumer Group hota hai — email-workers, sms-workers, push-workers. Har Consumer Group ke andar multiple consumers ho sakte hain - inhe worker
           bhi kehte hain, jo respective topic ke partitions se events parallelly consume aur process karte hain. Isse multiple events parallelly process ho sakte hain, jisse overall event 
           processing throughput improve hota hai.

         - In consumers ka high-level responsibility respective payloads ko corresponding external client/aggregator tak forward karna hota hai — API call (sync HTTP POST) ke through 
           taaki user ko Email, SMS ya Push Notification deliver ho sake.

         - Worker aggregator se success acknowledgement ka configured timeout tak synchronously wait karta hai. Agar aggregator se configured timeout ke andar success acknowledgement nahi milta, 
           toh worker configured retry policy ke according request retry karta hai. Retries ke beech Exponential Backoff + Jitter apply hota hai. Configured maximum retry attempts exhaust hone ke
           baad bhi request fail hoti hai, toh worker failed event ko DLT (Dead Letter Topic) mein publish kar deta hai.

         - Aggregator se success acknowledgement (`200 OK` ya `202 Accepted`) milne ke baad worker apne respective Kafka topic ka offset commit karta hai. Iske baad worker next available message 
           consume karke process karta hai.

           ## Important Nuance — 202 Accepted ≠ Delivered to User
              → 202 Accepted ka matlab sirf itna hai ki aggregator ne message receive kar liya hai ("maine SMS/Email/Push receive kar liya hai, main process karunga") — ye guarantee nahi ki
                message user tak pahunch gaya. Actual delivery ki tracking webhook ke through asynchronously hoti hai. Isi wajah se worker 202 Accepted aane pe hi offset commit kar deta hai, 
                actual delivery ka wait nahi karta — kyunki provider ne message ki responsibility le li hai.

